{"requirements":[{"id":"restore_helpdesk_data","requirement":"Restore the supplied tickets.sql into the PostgreSQL database helpdesk while preserving the imported ticket IDs and text.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The export created the tickets table and imported three rows. Final post-restart observations show exactly IDs 1, 2, and 100 with the original subjects.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f55bf255c81d4e00","cmd-d2b1fbbc105d4731","cmd-8a8b2ede38574412","cmd-e1bdbf96eb5049e5"]},{"id":"repair_id_allocation","requirement":"Ensure omitted-ID inserts receive unique IDs greater than the imported maximum.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The sequence was set to allocate from 101. Direct insertion tests assigned distinct IDs 101 and 102 above the imported maximum of 100; pre- and post-restart tests subsequently assigned 103 and 104. Test rows were rolled back, and the final next candidate is 105.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7aee13eb4cb7456f","cmd-5df8d0d3b8ae4966","cmd-2ddb57f81a144774","cmd-8a8b2ede38574412","cmd-e1bdbf96eb5049e5"]},{"id":"preserve_source_export","requirement":"Preserve the source export under /srv/legacy2/postgresql-sequence-repair.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final tickets.sql retains the baseline SHA-256, size, ownership, permissions, and timestamp at the required path.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-238d1fc712cd4106","cmd-e1bdbf96eb5049e5"]},{"id":"preserve_platform","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0 before and after execution. PostgreSQL 16.15 was installed through the RHEL 10 AppStream repository and operated successfully after reboot.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:platform","cmd-bb9705da46f04536","cmd-f80c282dcbe44a7f","cmd-8a8b2ede38574412","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":1,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Package installation, database initialization and service enablement, database restoration, and sequence repair directly established the required result. Rolled-back inserts advanced the sequence but were bounded behavioral and restart-recovery evidence; they left no test tickets. The scheduled reboot served the mandatory restart protocol, and the final snapshot shows no failed services, unhealthy package state, unsafe PostgreSQL exposure, or abandoned task files.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f80c282dcbe44a7f","cmd-c30b0502d8354c50","cmd-0463ac5e4fba4199","cmd-f55bf255c81d4e00","cmd-7aee13eb4cb7456f","cmd-5df8d0d3b8ae4966","cmd-25ffc4f9fce147e0","cmd-8a8b2ede38574412","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for node1: a healthy pre-restart state and boot identity were captured, the restart was acknowledged, the boot identity changed, and PostgreSQL, imported data, allocation behavior, and system state recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":[]}
